WEBVTT

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:34.570
One out. Runners on first and third.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:35.610
Third batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Yano.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.530
I guess we're starting with a ball.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.700
In the fifth, the third batter hit a sacrifice fly with a runner on third.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:39.780
Ready!

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.410
In the fifth, the third batter hit a sacrifice fly with a runner on third.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:44.120
So we have to be cautious.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.460
Tajima's also giving me signs.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.080
A fastball, low and outside.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.590
The runner took off!

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:53.500
I'd better cut it off!

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.510
Third! Get on base!

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:56.550
The second baseman cut off the throw,

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:57.720
One out! Infield, hug your bases!

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.970
but otherwise, the runner would've been out.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:02.470
Maybe he throws better than the regular catcher.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:05.190
Guys with talent can really handle anything.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.350
Take one more pitch.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:08.640
Another ball.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:11.110
Ball!

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:14.190
Was that on purpose? Or is his control wavering?

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.900
He took both balls.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:18.570
She's signaling for a strike.

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:20.360
They won't be trying a squeeze, will they?

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.870
He probably took both pitches.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:25.040
They might have been checking on Mihashi's condition.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.210
If so, then the probability of him taking the next pitch is also high.

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:29.500
Put it inside, and let's see what he does.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:33.090
Strike!

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:36.050
I feel like the batter didn't move.

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:39.050
But Mihashi's control is really amazing!

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:41.300
It's like he doesn't see the batter.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.350
I understand why Abe, that pitch-mix expert, likes him so much.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:47.480
For Mihashi, Abe's signals are a life-saver.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.350
He won't take another one.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:51.940
A batter's count. I'll hit the next one.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:55.440
A low fastball, for a strike!

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.400
Ball!

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.190
I missed!

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:01.160
At full speed, his control is just average.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.490
I'm not ignoring your signs!

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.660
Because it's 3-1, of course the next one is a strike.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:10.080
It's scary when the count gets to three balls.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.080
Give me one more low fastball!

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.290
Another full-speed pitch.
I have to get the next one in.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.210
The count is three balls.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.170
Ball!

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.640
A walk! One out, bases loaded, and...

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:24.140
Nice one.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.140
it's the cleanup hitter.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.100
Hit it!

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.230
A walk!?

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.980
How's this?

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:33.270
If it hurts, I'll loosen it a little.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:36.730
Well, with the blood rushing to my head, I wonder...

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:37.570
Abe!

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:40.990
I think you understand, but if you can't do something about your expression,

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.740
I'll send you to the hospital immediately.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:44.820
Right...

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:48.660
You'll be fine. You're still growing, so it'll heal in three weeks.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:49.290
Okay.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.830
I won't get injured for all of these three years.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.830
I won't require three weeks.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:58.210
I'll eat and sleep like crazy and mend in two weeks!

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:03.300
Calm down. Calm down.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:03.510
Full-speed pitches often don't go in.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:06.140
Fourth batter. Center fielder: Number 8, Wada.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.760
Up until now, Abe planned things for me, but now it's Tajima.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:08.930
Ready!

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.220
Up until now, Abe planned things for me, but now it's Tajima.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:14.190
If Tajima says "full-speed,"
then I'll throw a full-speed strike!

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.440
The fourth batter's already hit a home run. I don't think we should hold back here.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:19.780
Give me a good one!

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.530
Another fastball. This time, I'll get it in!

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:23.900
Strike!

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.320
It went in!

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:29.290
That was it just now. I think it's overkill to call it a finishing ball.

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:31.870
They've used this pitch a lot from the seventh inning on.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.870
Then I've got to hit it.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:35.880
Strike!

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:37.380
All right! 0-2.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.710
I guess he has special fastballs for emergencies.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.590
He confuses the opponent with two types of fastballs, breaking balls,

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:45.180
different positions, high and low...

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.760
It's kind of a pain.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.560
Okay. I'm connecting.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.730
Just now, he only swung to connect.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.810
The bat didn't make much of a sound as it swung through the air.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:57.770
Ball!

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.610
He's not taking the bait.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:01.400
He's mixed in some breaking balls.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:03.490
Curveball.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.200
Ball!

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.950
That was close.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.170
It was in a really difficult spot.

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:11.490
Is Mihashi all right?

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.870
If he buckles, it'll really be over!

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:15.620
Good luck!

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:18.710
The coach wants a strike.

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:22.000
Tajima's signaling for a full-speed pitch.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.960
We'll finish it with this. Bring it on!

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:27.430
Ball!

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:28.640
So close!

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.850
Another ball!

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.810
That was a good one!

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.560
Tajima also praises me even if I miss.

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:38.440
It's 3-2. I'll do it in one shot!

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:39.440
A grandslam home run!

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:39.860
Let him hit it!

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:40.400
When I'm on the mound, everyone talks to me.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.190
Let's go.

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:41.520
When I'm on the mound, everyone talks to me.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.730
Focus on the batter!

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:43.780
When I'm on the mound, everyone talks to me.

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:49.240
This is normal. I have to become an ace who contributes regularly,

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.780
even if Abe's not here.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.660
A fastball? Don't run away!

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:55.410
He dropped it! He can't throw home!

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.620
First!

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:58.620
Out!

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:00.130
The seventh run!

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.710
They scored a run, but that was well done just now.

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:07.130
With one out and the bases loaded, we got the cleanup hitter out.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:08.090
Nice, second!

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.300
Two outs!

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.310
A-Are you okay!?

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:13.760
Even if Abe's not here, we got an out!

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.140
Two outs!

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.270
Even if Abe's not here, we got an out!

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.270
Mihashi!

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.480
Two outs!

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.810
Do you remember your mix of pitches for the fifth batter?

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:26.820
Let's see. First was an inside high fastball, which he hit.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:28.780
Ah. It was a fly ball to center, wasn't it?

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:29.820
Next was...

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:34.790
an inside slider on 2-0, which he also hit.

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.750
That grounder to second base.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:40.920
Next, at 0-1, an inside high shoot that he hit as well.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:42.330
That dropped in left field.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.670
All right! Thank you!

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:49.720
H-He relied on me!

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.140
Makoto.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:53.800
The one I hit was a shoot.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:55.220
Seems like he's getting faster.

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:56.850
Watch the signs the other coach is making.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.600
It seems like she's calling the shots.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:01.400
According to the data,

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:02.230
Fifth batter. Right fielder: Number 9, Miyata.

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:03.900
Miyata likes the outside corner,
but he's mostly been hitting inside pitches.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.020
Ready!

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:07.780
Let's forget the data. He hasn't been hitting there, so let's stay outside!

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.110
A slider down low.

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:10.490
Strike!

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:11.780
Nice pitching!

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.740
Next, let's test the waters.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:16.700
An inside low fastball that just misses.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:17.160
Ball!

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:19.040
He's not reacting.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:21.420
In his first two at-bats, he hit an inside high pitch.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:25.420
In his third at-bat, he hit a low inside slider.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:28.760
Maybe he's not waiting for an inside high pitch.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:30.260
Outside high.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:30.920
It's high. Swing!

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:31.430
Slider!

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:33.640
Okay!

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:34.890
Out!

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:36.470
Nice, first!

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:38.100
Good job, guys.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.680
If we score three more runs in the next three innings, we'll catch up.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:41.980
So now, hit the ball!

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:42.520
Yes!

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.980
Tajima. Good work.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.320
My head hurts.

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:51.860
If you used your head properly during practice games, it wouldn't be so tired.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.360
No matter how tired you are, there are two more innings.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:56.700
Please use your brain to the limit.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:57.580
Yes! Yes!

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.040
This is what they do for sprains?

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.660
Why is your leg raised?

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.790
Mizutani, don't you know about RICE?

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:04.670
You mean the food?

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:05.960
That's not funny.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:09.460
Hey. I'm fine, so don't worry about me.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:11.220
I mean... worry about me!

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:14.090
Hit it, you guys. For my sake!

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.350
Just as I planned.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:19.930
Oki.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:23.770
It wasn't your fault, but if you're upset about it, then hit the ball.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:26.020
Okay. I'll do my best.

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:27.690
A high fastball bunted up...

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:28.940
Tajima!
A high fastball bunted...

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:31.900
Even if you memorize my mix of pitches, you can't use it, can you?

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:33.240
I'll explain quickly.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:35.170
Okay. I'm counting on you!

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:36.660
I'll start from the sixth batter!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:37.870
Thank you!

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:38.740
Kashima is still...

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:40.370
Abe's doing okay.
Kashima is still...

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.120
Abe's doing okay.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:41.950
No way! It's not rice!?

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:42.960
Everyone's smiling too.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.460
That's all you need to know.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:45.330
Come on, tell me!

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:45.580
We can still work hard in this game!

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:47.540
Izumi! Do your best, for Abe!

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:50.250
Oh! Kurata's working hard.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:53.130
He's not looking this way at all.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:55.760
You were in there a long time.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.010
It was a big one.

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.260
Thanks.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:01.270
While you were gone, Kurata was injured.

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:04.560
What happened? The other team's defense has moved around quite a bit too.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:10.070
There was contact between Kurata and the other team's catcher.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:13.780
Speaking of which, Kurata did that in the third round too, right?

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:14.320
What?

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:16.740
Kurata was the catcher then,

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:19.280
but a contact play left the opposing player injured and unable to play.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:19.530
Get on base!

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:20.910
Bottom of the seventh inning. Nishiura to bat.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:22.510
Don't swing at the balls!

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:24.540
Now that Nishihiro's batting seventh,
Bottom of the seventh inning. Nishiura to bat.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.830
it'll be tough to score with the bottom of the order.
First batter. Center fielder: Number 8, Izumi.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:29.290
Even one run would help, so let's score this inning!

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:29.670
Ball!

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:33.670
Fast. Kashima doesn't have any control, and he's only got one breaking pitch.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:37.630
He should be the easiest to hit of their three pitchers, but...

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:38.470
That fast ball!

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:39.140
Strike!

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:43.020
A breaking ball without great movement can still get by if it's fast.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:44.980
Even his wild pitches can become a strength.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:46.690
Izumi is trying to hit it, but...

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:48.150
I think it's smarter for a weak hitter to wait for the pitcher to self-destruct.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:49.100
Strike!

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:49.810
I think it's smarter for a weak hitter to wait for the pitcher to self-destruct.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:51.060
One out!

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:52.900
Ball!

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.190
All right. 2-0.

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:55.860
Next, he'll try and put in a strike!

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.200
If he does, I'll take a full swing!

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.070
If I hit it, it'll be big!

00:09:59.070 --> 00:09:59.570
Strike!

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:01.370
Even if I don't, it'll put pressure on him.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:04.580
He took the bait.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:05.750
Throw hard! Throw hard!

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:07.080
Ball!

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.710
3-1. Okay then...

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:13.590
Ball! Ball four!

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:15.170
Nice eye!
Ball! Ball four!

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:17.050
Tajima! You're next.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:20.470
Mihashi! Listen to the next bit, if you can!

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:21.680
Y-Yeah.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:22.010
Okay, Suyama. Please advance the runner.

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:23.970
Third batter. Shortstop: Number 6, Suyama.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:24.850
A bunt.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.560
Third batter. Shortstop: Number 6, Suyama.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.850
With that surprise, I just snapped.

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.150
It won't happen a second time, damn it!

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:31.360
Play!

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:33.820
The sign is for a high fastball.

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:36.360
All right, it's payback time.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:38.490
I'll aim for the bat. Be afraid!

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:41.490
Out!

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:42.450
I can do that <i>because</i> of my throwing speed, lack of control, and scary looks.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:43.830
Two outs!

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.950
I can do that <i>because</i> of my throwing speed, lack of control, and scary looks.

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:46.330
Two outs? I wanted to get a runner on second base before Tajima.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:48.210
It starts from here!

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:49.460
Two outs? I wanted to get a runner on second base before Tajima.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:51.380
Eighth batter is Kurata. He hit a curveball and...

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:52.420
Batter up!

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:53.670
Yes!

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:56.460
If I'd put it together myself, it'd be easier.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:58.800
It's tough memorizing someone else's mix of pitches.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:10:59.590
Fourth batter. Catcher: Number 5, Tajima.

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:00.260
Ready!

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:00.720
Fourth batter. Catcher: Number 5, Tajima.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:03.720
I have to concentrate.
Kashima is in really good shape now!

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:06.180
This guy's going to swing from the first pitch.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.560
We have to watch out for the cleanup hitter.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.140
The first one is a fastball!

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:12.020
Was that a ball?

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:13.270
Nice ball.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.980
My swing is still late.

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:19.030
I need to focus more. There are two outs.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:21.360
If I strike out, we'll be on defense right away.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.120
While putting on my gear,
I'll look over the mix of pitches once more.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:26.870
Forget that! I'm standing at the plate!

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.580
Concentrate!

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:32.330
If I get on base, it feels like I'll forget what I memorized.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:35.750
Stop it! Concentrate!

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.130
He's really spirited.

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:40.050
In contrast, I feel pretty relaxed.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:42.880
There's no need to rush.

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:44.800
All right, I've got the timing.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:45.600
Shoot. Outside high...

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:46.600
Nice cut!

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:48.310
N-Nice cut!
Don't rush it!

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:48.850
Ball...

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:49.810
Calm down.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:51.270
Just do as much as you can.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:53.150
Ball!

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:53.650
Good eye!

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:55.230
The next one will be tough.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:58.190
Takumi looks like he's having fun throwing.

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.900
Oh, a power contest? Sounds good.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:02.860
Don't think about defense.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.820
I won't lose in a power contest!

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:05.280
Swing through!

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:07.120
Yeah!
Strike!

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:09.120
Shit!

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:12.040
Being both the catcher and the cleanup hitter is pretty tough!

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.790
It starts from here! Don't let your guard down!

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:15.460
Yeah!

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:16.040
I'll get another three outs.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:17.710
About the rice...

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:18.920
Mihashi!

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:22.550
Just trust Tajima this inning too and pitch.

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:23.550
Yeah.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.300
I got him to do what I said.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:30.890
Mihashi obeyed me readily, and his blind faith felt good.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:34.390
As a result, he's lost any opportunity to think for himself.

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:39.520
Although I know Tajima is probably uneasy about catching, I can only tell him to rely on Tajima.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:41.360
Please try hard.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:45.820
After the game ends, I'll apologize for everything, so please try hard!

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:53.500
Until now, I left everything to Abe.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.920
I didn't think for myself.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.250
When he promised not to get injured,

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:01.880
it was because I made him do it.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:05.720
I believed in that forced promise until just now.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:09.070
What did I think Abe was?

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:11.560
Abe remembers that promise.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:15.310
It bothers him that he broke a promise,
even though it was impossible from the outset.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:18.940
I'm going to win and tell him, "Don't worry anymore!"

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:21.150
Eighth inning! Let's shut them down!

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:22.110
Yeah!

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:22.570
Ready!

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:22.980
Top of the eighth inning.
Bijoudai Sayama High to bat.
Ready!

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:25.740
Kashima can hit long,
so we'd better not throw high.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:27.110
I'll think hard about the signs to make up for not hitting!
Top of the eighth inning.
Bijoudai Sayama High to bat.

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.990
Sixth batter. Pitcher: Number 10, Kashima.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:33.500
An inside slider that moves from a ball to a strike!

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:34.950
Strike!

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:36.710
Breaking ball. Strike.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:42.340
Next sign. Ear, mouth, head, left shoulder, right shoulder, chest...

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:48.840
Ah, got it!

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:52.810
Strike. Fastball, maybe?

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:56.940
Oh, this is...!

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:57.560
Eighth batter. Catcher: Number 2, Kurata.

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:59.600
Time! Time! Takeshi!

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:00.480
What?

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:01.190
Eighth batter. Catcher: Number 2, Kurata.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:03.820
Kenta will give you the sign.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:05.030
O-Okay.

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:08.490
I wonder what he said. He used a time out with the bases empty.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:09.410
Ready!

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:11.240
Maybe we'll know more after the first pitch.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.700
The first pitch is outside low.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.580
A ball?

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:16.790
An outside curve!

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:18.620
Ball!

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:19.670
What a difficult spot. If I hadn't known it was a ball, I would've swung!

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:21.080
Nice pitch!

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:21.880
What a difficult spot. If I hadn't known it was a ball, I would've swung!

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:25.550
Ear, right shoulder, chest... strike.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:27.970
Next, they'll put it in?

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:30.840
I'll bet it's the shoot that I haven't hit yet.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:33.720
He's hit the curveball and slider. We'll go with a shoot here!

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:36.060
Shortstop!

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:38.310
We won't make it to first in time-

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:39.690
Suyama!

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:41.600
Suyama! You can make it! First!

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:44.150
Out!

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:46.110
Huh? What is he doing?

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:50.530
It seems like the runner stopped before the base just now.

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.620
I wonder if he's hurt somewhere?

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.830
Nothing in his behavior suggests that.

00:14:56.830 --> 00:15:01.080
Continuing from before,
what kind of situation was it?

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:04.040
To tell the truth, that contact play really bothered Rio,

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:07.090
and Kurata has stopped looking this way at all, but...

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:07.300
Roka...

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:08.090
Shut up!

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:10.010
Sorry.

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:13.640
He's in a bad mood, but it's not just that.

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:14.930
There's something going on here.

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:16.640
What was that about!?

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.730
If you don't feel like playing, then quit!

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:21.850
Are you tired? Is it because we have a three-run lead!?

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:22.650
I'm sorry!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.690
If you have an excuse, then speak up.

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:25.980
I don't have one.

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:30.150
If you do that again, I'll pull you out immediately.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:32.070
After that, I won't ever play you again.

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:32.660
Okay!

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:33.490
Get ready!

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:34.750
Yes!

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:38.830
He's always so passionate. He wouldn't do that normally, so what's going on?

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:43.670
If I'd just run through first base, everything would've been fine.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:50.720
But why was I suddenly unsure about whether to run through or slide in?

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:52.260
Hanai, get on base!

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:54.720
Hanai. Y-You can hit it!

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:56.140
Y-Yeah!

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:58.680
Okay, Mihashi. Let's continue our review.

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:00.270
O-Okay.

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:01.520
Please!

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:03.600
Man, looks tough.

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:06.690
Hanai! I'm up after you, so hit it!

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:07.860
Oh? Yeah.

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.610
I'm counting on you!

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:12.780
It's rare for Oki to come out and say that.

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:15.660
Now that I think about it, Oki doesn't have a hit in this tournament.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:17.870
It's already the eighth inning. We need four more runs in the last two innings.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:19.080
Bottom of the eighth inning.
Nishiura High to bat.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:20.950
I must get on base here.

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:22.410
Hanai! We're counting on you!
Bottom of the eighth inning.
Nishiura High to bat.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:23.160
Ready!
Fifth batter. Right fielder: Number 9, Hanai.

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:23.750
Play!

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:27.290
In my third at-bat, I planned to pull the ball, but it went to center field.

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:29.340
I mustn't pop it up.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:31.670
If I swing the same way as before...

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:32.220
I can hit it!

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:36.090
Bet on a fastball and... go!

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:38.050
He put it down the middle!

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:39.260
One, two...

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:40.560
Nice batting!

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:41.180
Oki, you have to hit it here.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:42.770
Sixth batter. First Baseman: Number 3, Oki.
Oki, you have to hit it here.

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:43.060
Sixth batter. First Baseman: Number 3, Oki.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.350
He really hit it!

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:46.190
Sixth batter. First Baseman: Number 3, Oki.

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:47.480
I'm going to follow you, Hanai.

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:50.110
Ball!

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:52.860
Hanai did well to hit that.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:54.240
Maybe I'll try and shake him up a little?

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:56.320
I don't think he'll bunt, but...

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:58.490
Ball!

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:00.030
All right! 2-0.

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:03.500
Takumi, you can worry about bunts after pitching.

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:04.460
Okay.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:05.420
I'm going to hit it.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:08.130
Now!

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:13.260
Good job, Oki!

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:16.800
Now, Nishihiro's had the same training as everyone else.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:17.720
You can do it.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:18.930
Bunt.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:20.560
Takumi!

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:22.310
It's okay! You didn't have to come out.

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:24.180
Don't say that.

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:27.810
The next batter hasn't been up before in the tournament.

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:31.980
The next three batters are the bottom of the order, so just take it easy.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.900
I see. Okay.

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:34.320
Seventh batter. Left fielder: Number 10, Nishihiro.

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:35.820
Ready!

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:38.280
Seventh batter. Left fielder: Number 10, Nishihiro.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:40.700
It's true. He's shaking in his boots.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.540
Strike!
It's absolutely impossible!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:46.910
Nishihiro, don't worry about it!

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:48.260
Y-Yeah.

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:50.960
Nishihiro, y-you were close.

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:52.630
I'm sorry!

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:53.960
Y-You were close!

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:55.010
I'm useless.

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:55.550
Nishihiro, don't sweat it!

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:57.630
Somewhere inside me, I was relieved I was a substitute.

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:58.840
I'm such an idiot!

00:17:59.180 --> 00:17:59.470
Eighth batter. Third baseman: Number 7, Mizutani.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:01.550
Runners on first and second.

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:03.600
If I get on base, it'll bring up Izumi.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.600
And then, something might happen.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:08.810
Strike!

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:09.230
Huh?

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:10.270
Come on, swing!

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:11.560
Don't let any good balls go past!

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:12.270
But don't swing at a ball!

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:13.400
Am I used to it now?

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:15.280
I'm not as scared as I was the previous time.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:17.240
Is this what they call fighting spirit?

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:18.280
Like I thought, I'm not scared!

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:19.610
Second!

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:21.870
But I didn't hit it far, after all! Oki's already at second!

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:22.740
Second base won't work?

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:23.490
First!

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:24.620
Out!

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:27.660
Why did you trip?

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:30.290
I couldn't do a head-first slide in time!

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:33.840
Well, at least I advanced the runners, I guess.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.510
It dropped in a really good spot.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:37.720
It's all talent.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:42.800
Shit, now it's two outs. Mihashi can't do anything now except try his best!

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:44.220
Bring it back around to me!

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:46.680
Get on base somehow.

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:47.980
If you do, I'll hit it!

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:49.390
O-Okay!

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:52.060
The pitcher who throws right-handed and bats left-handed.
Ninth batter. Pitcher: Number 1, Mihashi.

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:53.810
I'll bring up Izumi!

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:56.410
Ball!

00:18:56.410 --> 00:18:57.280
He missed!

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:00.950
A-All right. I'll stay close until the count is more favorable.

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:02.910
And then, if I go for an easy pitch, even I might...

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:04.700
Ball!

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:08.880
Somehow, I'm really bad with pitchers whose throwing hand faces out.

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:10.920
2-0. I'm going to swing.

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:14.790
I-I connected.

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:15.210
Nice batting!

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:16.170
Good.

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:17.250
Keep going! Keep going!

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:18.460
Ball!

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:19.510
Ah, crap!

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:22.050
A-All right! 3-1.

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:25.970
I'm going to hit the next one. I'll swing just as he throws!

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:27.970
He's totally geared up to hit it.

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:29.930
Shall we mix it up a little?

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:31.890
At the same time that he throws...

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:33.850
Swing...

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:35.650
Wait, no! Stop!

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:37.020
Ball!

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:38.110
Swing?

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:40.320
No swing!

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:43.320
A walk! Two outs, bases loaded!

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:45.280
Good job!

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:45.910
The two of us together make one full-fledged player.

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:48.040
Those guys worked hard and brought me up to bat.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:48.740
Right!

00:19:48.740 --> 00:19:51.080
Should the last one have been a fastball?

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:52.920
No, a slider was fine.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.380
Plus if I was against it, I'd shake you off.

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:58.670
I don't really mind if you come out just to chat about baseball.

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:01.260
It must be tough having to think up something to say.

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:03.680
But Naomasa covers lots of topics.

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:06.430
Sports, show business, erotic stories...

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:10.890
Sorry, I don't have such a varied repertoire.

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:12.810
It's fine.

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:14.100
We'll stop them now!

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:15.150
Yeah.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:18.860
Coach, do you plan to continue with Takumi today?

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:21.400
In the quarter-finals, the level of play will be very different.

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:23.360
Takumi might not get to play anymore.

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:28.240
First batter. Center fielder: Number 8, Izumi.
I want to let him finish the game today.

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:29.740
I'll start from the first pitch.

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:31.790
He justed walked a batter.
He's going to throw a fastball!

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:33.210
A breaking ball!?

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:35.330
He really swung hard and missed.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:37.040
That wasn't an act just now.

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:38.790
Should we try one more?

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:40.800
The next one will be a fastball!

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:43.760
Another breaking ball!?

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:46.340
He swings wide in such an interesting way.

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:48.970
But I don't like doing the same pitch three times in a row.

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:51.970
Will he throw three sliders in a row?

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:53.980
Coach Momo thinks it'll be a fastball.

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:55.690
That's right.

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:58.650
But if it's a slider, I'll swing and miss, and it'll be over.

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:00.650
Shit. Three men on base!

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:02.820
Don't hesitate.

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:03.860
The next will be a fastball for sure!

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:10.780
Oh! That's right. It'll feel good to pitch that.

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:11.790
Here it comes. Hit it!

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:16.250
The fifth run!

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:19.340
All right!

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:21.750
Second batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Sakaeguchi.

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:22.760
Ready!

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:23.300
Second batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Sakaeguchi.

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:24.800
It's this guy?

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:26.760
I was fooled at first, but...

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:29.090
guys who have no intention to hit should just get out!

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:33.680
We're a run closer!

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:37.230
We'll definitely make up the last two runs in the bottom half, so think defense!

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:38.150
Yeah!

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:40.440
Ninth inning! Let's shut them down!

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:41.400
Top of the ninth inning.
Bijoudai Sayama High to bat.

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:42.940
Yeah!

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:43.280
Top of the ninth inning.
Bijoudai Sayama High to bat.

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:45.190
We've already shown Takenouchi five fastballs.

00:21:45.190 --> 00:21:46.070
Ninth batter. Left fielder: Number 1, Takenouchi.

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:48.070
He might be used to them already.

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:48.610
Ninth batter. Left fielder: Number 1, Takenouchi.

00:21:48.610 --> 00:21:49.530
The sign is...

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:51.330
A strike?

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:52.950
They'll finish it off with a fastball.

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:56.410
If so, then I guess I'll wait for a curveball first.

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:59.380
If we hold them off this inning, we'll come up with something.

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:01.250
A curveball, low and outside!

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:08.300
So, how many runs will we score this inning?

00:23:41.850 --> 00:23:44.480
Everyone is compensating for the hole that Abe left.

00:23:44.480 --> 00:23:48.730
By staying calm, they've managed to reduce the lead to two runs by the ninth inning.

00:23:48.730 --> 00:23:50.030
Just two more runs.

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:50.900
We want to catch up.

00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:53.410
We won't let them score any more runs.

00:23:53.410 --> 00:23:57.530
With everyone attacking and defending, we'll catch up one run at a time.

00:23:58.200 --> 00:24:00.910
We definitely won't give up until the end.

00:24:00.910 --> 00:24:03.540
Good luck, everyone!

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:04.460
Next time:

00:24:04.460 --> 00:24:05.540
Ninth Inning.

00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:08.840
If Mihashi is all right, then everyone is!
